KBlueProximity
--------------

Configuration is stored in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kblueproximity/ as ConfigObj
files (default: ~/.config/kblueproximity/).

On first run, existing settings from legacy directories ~/.kblueproximity/
and ~/.blueproximity/ are copied if present.

Pair a Bluetooth device with BlueZ first, then set its MAC address in
Preferences. Default lock/unlock commands use loginctl; Plasma can also
use the freedesktop ScreenSaver interface via qdbus6.

As a modern autostart alternative, a user systemd unit is installed at:
/usr/lib/systemd/user/kblueproximity.service

Enable it with:
  systemctl --user daemon-reload
  systemctl --user enable --now kblueproximity.service
